rule WEBPERF202 "unbounded-fetchall" {
  lang python
  severity error

  find c: call where c.text ~ /\.fetchall\(\)/
  report c "fetchall() loads every matching row into memory in one response"

  example fire python """
    rows = cur.fetchall()  #~ error
  """
  example clean python """
    rows = cur.fetchmany(100)
  """
  example notapplicable markdown """
    Prose has no queries.
  """
  explain """
    A handler that reads a whole result set grows its memory and response time with the table, so one large table makes every request slow (WEBPERF, server side).
    ## Remedy
    Page the query with LIMIT and OFFSET (or a keyset), or read it with `fetchmany(n)` or a cursor iterator and stream the rows.
  """
}
